escription_full":"Automatic Data Processing, Inc. provides cloud-based human capital management (HCM) solutions worldwide. It operates in two segments, Employer Services and Professional Employer Organization (PEO). The Employer Services segment offers strategic, cloud-based platforms, and human resources (HR) outsourcing solutions. This segment's offerings include RUN Powered by ADP, a software platform for small business payroll, HR, and compliance; ADP Workforce Now, a HCM solution used across mid-sized and large businesses to manage employees; and ADP Lyric HCM, a solution for HR management, payroll, workforce management, talent, and data analytics. Its PEO Services segment provides HR outsourcing solutions under ADP TotalSource name to businesses through a co-employment model. This segment also provides guidance, user-friendly technology, comprehensive employee benefits, and a risk management, safety, and workers' compensation program. The company was founded in 1949 and is headquartered in Roseland, New Jersey.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Maria  Black | President, CEO & DIrector | Age 51 | Compensation: $4.8M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 67K people. Revenue per employee of $328K ranks in the below the sector median among Technology peers, improving at 6%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $78K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 15\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Automatic Data Processing, Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $119.8B market cap on $21.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 87% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 78-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $5.2B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 24 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.23\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 13\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 3.9% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.5858437822287367},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $10.3M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (35% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 21% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","42 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Technology peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Did Payroll Data Just Shift ADP Stock's Investment Narrative?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/did-payroll-data-just-shift-180747786.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793902067.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is Automatic Data Processing (ADP) Priced Right for Its Cash Flow?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/automatic-data-processing-adp-priced-151857312.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793891937.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Automatic Data Processing (ADP) Faces A 13% Fair Value Gap As Jobs Data And Earnings Impress","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/automatic-data-processing-adp-faces-141157869.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793887917.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.935,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"ADP Canada Pay Insights: Pay for Job-Stayers Was Up 3.0% in October","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/adp-canada-pay-insights-pay-131500000.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793885243.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.226,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Automatic Data Processing (NASDAQ:ADP) Stock: Insider Michael Bonarti Sells 7,487 Shares","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/automatic-data-processing-nasdaqadp-stock-insider