ith about $576.0M traded a day.","In past sell-offs it fell 39% in the 2020 crash, 20% in the 2022 bear market and 32% in 2008."],"val":["The stock trades only 7% below its DCF fair value of $325, a thin margin of safety.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 37%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $255 to $428 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 6% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 4.4% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 5.0% (vs the 8% bar).","The 15 covering analysts target $298 on average, 2% below the price.","The price implies 5.6% annual cash-flow growth, 1pp less than the model expects."],"prof":["ROIC of 87% clears the cost of capital of 8.5% by 78pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.49).","It converts 24% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.23x.","ROE of 73% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (10.5x equity multiplier).","It spends 4.7% of revenue on R&D and 1.1% on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is conservative at 0.1x net debt to EBITDA ($4.2B of cash against $5.0B of debt), with interest covered 13.5x."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 6.8% over 3 years, 7.9% over 5 years and 6.5% over 10 years.","At current returns, reinvesting 4% of profits supports about 3.2% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 12.5% a year over five years.","Capex runs only 0.3x depreciation (0.9% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 31, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business.","Analysts expect 9.4% long-term annual earnings growth."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.1%), and institutions hold 92%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (34 sales, net $10.3M sold).","It returns 3.9% a year to shareholders (1.7% in buybacks and 2.2% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 1.2% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","It has paid a dividend for 42 consecutive years, raising it 10.8% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 67,000 employees, each generates about $328K of revenue, in line with the Technology median, and productivity has risen 5.8% a year.","That works out to $78K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $4.8M (15x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $4K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":80,"head":"Watch: LEAN BUY-rated, but only 7% below fair value; it becomes a buy below $276.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 55, gates 15/26)","ROIC 86.8% vs WACC 8.5%","FCF margin 23.9%","Revenue grew 7.9%/yr over 5y","Net debt/EBITDA 0.1x"],"cons":[],"flags":[],"need":["only 7% below fair value"],"buy_below":276.05,"vc":{"base":324.77,"base_src":"dcf","bear":255.28,"bull":428.0,"alt_median":166.92,"n_alt":3,"gap":0.9457,"dispersion":0.3689,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (37% dispersion)","DCF is 95% above the other models' median ($167)"]},"med":{"pe":26.7484,"ev_ebitda":16.351,"pfcf":25.4376,"pb":3.7763,"roic":0.0752,"gross_margin":0.4714,"fcf_margin":0.1275,"div_yield":0.0129}},"ticker":"ADP","date":"2026-11-06"}